  "event_id": "E006",
  "text": "Permit and Plan Review Fees for the Building Department | Mesa County\nSkip to main content\nStage 1 Fire Restrictions enacted\nEffective beginning 12:01 a.m. Friday, Sept. 4, 2026, until further notice. These restrictions apply to all private land and BLM managed public lands within the boundaries of the Grand Junction Field Office. For more information visit the Fire Restrictions webpage.\nTranslate\nMain navigation\nMENU\nMENU\nResident Resources\nBusiness Resources\nDepartments and Services\nContact Us\nJobs\nADA\nEvents\nNews\nTranslate\nBreadcrumb\nHome\nDepartments and Services\nCommunity Development\nBuilding Department\nBuilding Department Fees\nPermit and Plan Review Fees for the Building Department\nNotice\nPermit issuance after 4:30 p.m. will be on a limited basis.\nNo multiple permits will be issued after 4:30 p.m.\nAdopted Fee Schedule (PDF)\nResidential and Interior Remodel Permit Fee Calculator\nNew construction\nTo determine the applicable building permit fee for new construction, including additions, refer to the Building Department Fee Schedule.  Locate Table 3A- Building Valuation Data for the correct permit fee. Valuations will be rounded up in all cases.\nLocate the use of the building from the left column.\nLocate the construction type from one of the vertical columns. This will give you the per square foot construction costs.\nFor residential one and two family construction and their related structures, use the VB (far right) column for square foot construction costs.\nDetermine the total valuation of the project by multiplying the area in square feet of the structure by the dollar amount indicated on the table.\nRemodel work\nDetermine the applicable building permit fee for remodel work and all other building up-grades from Mesa County Building Department Fee Schedule, based on the valuation of the project.\nMiscellaneous fees\nOther fees may be assessed depending on the scope of the project.\nBuilding Department\nAdopted Codes and Regulations\nAgenda and Decisions\nBuilding Advisory Committee\nBuilding Guides\nBuilding Guides in Spanish\nContact Us\nContractor Licensing\nFrequently Asked Questions\nIECC Energy Code Requirements\nIndustry Resources\nInspection and Policy Information\nPermit and Plan Review Fees\nBuilding Permit Fee Estimator\nPermit Records 1988 to Current\nPermit Records Pre 1988\nPermit Requirements\nProposed Adopted Codes and Regulations\nReports and Statistics\nState Electrical and Plumbing Licensing\nTraining Opportunities\nWildfire Code\nContact Us\nTelephone\nDepartment Directory\nContact Information\nContact Information\nComments and Feedback\nGet in Touch\nMesa County is committed to providing equitable access to our services to the public. For accessibility assistance with any part of this website, including but not limited to any documents on this website, please visit the Mesa County ADA Compliance webpage for contact information.\n© 2026 Mesa County, Colorado\nADA Policy\nPrivacy Policy\nPowered by Interpersonal Frequency",
